---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
export const prerender = false;
---

<BaseLayout
	title="That link did not work"
	eyebrow="Sign in"
	crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Sign in', href: '/sign-in' }, { name: 'Link expired' }]}
>
	<section class="band band-tight">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>That link did not work</h2>
				<p>
					Sign-in links work once and expire after fifteen minutes, so this is usually one of two
					things: it has already been used, or it sat in the inbox too long. Some mail scanners
					also follow links before you do, which spends them.
				</p>
				<p>
					Nothing is wrong with your account and nothing has been logged against it.
					<a href="/sign-in">Ask for a new link</a>.
				</p>
				<p style="font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted)">
					We deliberately do not say which of those happened. Telling whoever is holding a link
					whether it is merely expired or belongs to a real account is the one thing that page
					could give away.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
